      en: "High Wycombe is a large town in Buckinghamshire, England, situated on the River Wye. It has a population of 120,000 (2021) and covers an area of 64 square kilometres. The town grew rapidly during the Industrial Revolution, becoming a centre for furniture manufacturing, especially chairs. Today, its economy is diversified with a strong service sector, including the headquarters of companies like Johnson & Johnson and the Buckinghamshire Healthcare NHS Trust. High Wycombe is located in the Chiltern Hills, an Area of Outstanding Natural Beauty, providing scenic landscapes. Key landmarks include the 18th-century Guildhall, the Wycombe Museum, and the historic Hughenden Manor, a National Trust property. The town is well-connected by the M40 motorway and Chiltern Railways, offering fast commutes to London.",
